  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: The forecast remains on track. An upper\nlevel low continues its journey around the PacNW, bringing cooler\ntemperatures, strong winds and precipitation potential. A strong \npressure gradient is developing across the area, resulting in \nstrong winds across the area and temperatures ranging from the \nupper 60s in northern Nevada to the low 80s in central Nevada. \nStrong winds are expected to continue through Sunday, particularly\nin White Pine, northeast Nye and southeast Elko Counties. \nMoisture availability starting Sunday has been trending downward \nthe last several forecasts and precipitation potential has \nnoticeably decreased along with it. Isolated to scattered showers \nand thunderstorms continue to be forecast across much of the \nforecast area for Sunday but accumulation totals have dropped to \n0.05 inches at best, with most of the area expecting a trace or \nless. Precipitation chances dry out by Monday morning, allowing a \ndry but cool day, with high temperatures in the 70s. Unsettled \nweather is expected to continue for mid week even as temperatures \nwarm back into the 80s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in cool\ntemperatures and strong winds through the weekend. Weekend storm\nconfidence continues to be moderate, with low confidence in storm\npotential next week. No changes from the NBM.",
